RunInfo: >
  Requires independent 160 GeV mu+ p and mu+ n samples in PP, PM, MP, and
  MM helicities, with POSNLO and NEGNLO generated separately.
NumEvents: 100000
NeedsCrossSection: yes
Beams: [[ANTIMUON, PROTON], [ANTIMUON, NEUTRON]]
Energies: [[160.0, 0.938272], [160.0, 0.939565]]
Description: >
  Reconstructs Lorentz-invariant DIS and identified pi+/-, K+/- kinematics
  from the highest-energy prompt scattered positive muon. Event-aggregated
  ordinary, inverse-depolarization, and same-event covariance-proxy yields
  are filled in the ten published x bins. The campaign postprocessor forms
  sigma_UU=(p+n)/2 and sigma_LL=0.925(p+n)/2, uses the finite-muon-mass
  COMPASS depolarization factor with R1998, and sets eta*A2 to zero. HEPData
  v1 is the numerical authority; differences from the paper TeX table are
  retained in a checksum-pinned audit.
